<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Derivation of Bayesian Estimator and Uncertainty</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As described in the main text, the Bayesian framework is built on two quantities. The first is <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(R)</annotation></semantics></math>, the average of <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> over the joint posterior for all the questions:</p>
<table id="A1.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu(R)=\int_{\Delta}d\bm{\pi}_{1}\cdots\int_{\Delta}d\bm{\pi}_{M}\,\bar{\pi}\prod_{\alpha=1}^{M}{\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}|\bm{R}_{\alpha})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mi>𝒫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(R)=\int_{\Delta}d\bm{\pi}_{1}\cdots\int_{\Delta}d\bm{\pi}_{M}\,\bar{\pi}\prod_{\alpha=1}^{M}{\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}|\bm{R}_{\alpha}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the integration region <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability simplex defined as the set of all possible <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional vectors <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{p}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{C}p_{k}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{C}p_{k}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. The second is the variance <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> associated with our Bayesian estimator,</p>
<table id="A1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma^{2}(R)=\int_{\Delta}d\bm{\pi}_{1}\cdots\int_{\Delta}d\bm{\pi}_{M}\,(\bar{\pi}-\mu(R))^{2}\prod_{\alpha=1}^{M}{\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}|\bm{R}_{\alpha})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mi>𝒫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}(R)=\int_{\Delta}d\bm{\pi}_{1}\cdots\int_{\Delta}d\bm{\pi}_{M}\,(\bar{\pi}-\mu(R))^{2}\prod_{\alpha=1}^{M}{\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}|\bm{R}_{\alpha}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our derivation of closed-form expressions for <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> builds on the generalized (<math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>) and original (<math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=1</annotation></semantics></math>) Laplace rule of succession theory from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jaynes [2003]</a></cite>, recovering those results in the special case of a single question (<math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=1</annotation></semantics></math>). We start with Bayes’ rule for each row of <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}|\bm{R}_{\alpha})=\frac{{\cal P}(\bm{R}_{\alpha}|\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}){\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha})}{{\cal P}(\bm{R}_{\alpha})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}|\bm{R}_{\alpha})=\frac{{\cal P}(\bm{R}_{\alpha}|\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}){\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha})}{{\cal P}(\bm{R}_{\alpha})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The likelihood <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal P}(\bm{R}_{\alpha}|\bm{\pi}_{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal P}(\bm{R}_{\alpha}|\bm{\pi}_{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-category multinomial distribution over <math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> trials, with the probability distribution function:</p>
<table id="A1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal P}(\bm{R}_{\alpha}|\pi_{\alpha})=\frac{N!}{n_{\alpha 0}!n_{\alpha 1}!\cdots n_{\alpha C}!}\prod_{k=0}^{C}\left(\pi_{\alpha k}\right)^{n_{\alpha k}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>!</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>!</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal P}(\bm{R}_{\alpha}|\pi_{\alpha})=\frac{N!}{n_{\alpha 0}!n_{\alpha 1}!\cdots n_{\alpha C}!}\prod_{k=0}^{C}\left(\pi_{\alpha k}\right)^{n_{\alpha k}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\alpha k}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\delta_{k,R_{\alpha i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\alpha k}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\delta_{k,R_{\alpha i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{n}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒏</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{n}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is the vector with elements <math id="A1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\alpha k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\alpha k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Kronecker delta.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The prior <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen as the conjugate prior of the multinomial, a Dirichlet distribution <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha})\sim\text{Dir}(\bm{n}_{\alpha}^{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Dir</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒏</mi><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha})\sim\text{Dir}(\bm{n}_{\alpha}^{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, with concentration parameter vector <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{n}_{\alpha}^{0}=(n_{\alpha 0}^{0},\ldots,n_{\alpha C}^{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒏</mi><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{n}_{\alpha}^{0}=(n_{\alpha 0}^{0},\ldots,n_{\alpha C}^{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hayden and Armitage [2025]</a></cite> A uniform prior (no prior knowledge) sets <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\alpha k}^{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\alpha k}^{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Prior information from an earlier <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\times D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\times D</annotation></semantics></math> matrix <math id="A1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (with <math id="A1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{0}_{\alpha i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{0}_{\alpha i}</annotation></semantics></math> as the category for the <math id="A1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th trial of the <math id="A1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>th question) can be incorporated as:</p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{0}_{\alpha k}=1+\sum_{i=1}^{D}\delta_{k,R^{0}_{\alpha i}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{0}_{\alpha k}=1+\sum_{i=1}^{D}\delta_{k,R^{0}_{\alpha i}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The Dirichlet prior is:</p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha})=\frac{\Gamma(1+C+D)}{\prod_{k=0}^{C}\Gamma(n^{0}_{\alpha k})}\prod_{k=0}^{C}\left(\pi_{\alpha k}\right)^{n^{0}_{\alpha k}-1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha})=\frac{\Gamma(1+C+D)}{\prod_{k=0}^{C}\Gamma(n^{0}_{\alpha k})}\prod_{k=0}^{C}\left(\pi_{\alpha k}\right)^{n^{0}_{\alpha k}-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{C}n^{0}_{\alpha k}=1+C+D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{C}n^{0}_{\alpha k}=1+C+D</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The normalization constant <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal P}(\bm{R}_{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal P}(\bm{R}_{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal P}(\bm{R}_{\alpha})=\int_{\Delta}d\bm{p}\,{\cal P}(\bm{R}_{\alpha}|\bm{p}){\cal P}(\bm{p})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal P}(\bm{R}_{\alpha})=\int_{\Delta}d\bm{p}\,{\cal P}(\bm{R}_{\alpha}|\bm{p}){\cal P}(\bm{p}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">and since the Dirichlet is the conjugate prior, the posterior is <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}|\bm{R}_{\alpha})\sim\text{Dir}(\bm{\nu}_{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Dir</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝂</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}|\bm{R}_{\alpha})\sim\text{Dir}(\bm{\nu}_{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\nu}_{\alpha}=\bm{n}_{\alpha}+\bm{n}^{0}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝂</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒏</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒏</mi><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\nu}_{\alpha}=\bm{n}_{\alpha}+\bm{n}^{0}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. The posterior distribution is:</p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}|\bm{R}_{\alpha})=\frac{\Gamma(T)}{\prod_{k=0}^{C}\Gamma(\nu_{\alpha k})}\prod_{k=0}^{C}\left(\pi_{\alpha k}\right)^{\nu_{\alpha k}-1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}|\bm{R}_{\alpha})=\frac{\Gamma(T)}{\prod_{k=0}^{C}\Gamma(\nu_{\alpha k})}\prod_{k=0}^{C}\left(\pi_{\alpha k}\right)^{\nu_{\alpha k}-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\equiv\sum_{k=0}^{C}\nu_{\alpha k}=1+C+D+N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">≡</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\equiv\sum_{k=0}^{C}\nu_{\alpha k}=1+C+D+N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The moment generating function <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(t)=\langle\exp(\bar{\pi}t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(t)=\langle\exp(\bar{\pi}t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\Phi(t)&amp;=\int_{\Delta}d\bm{\pi}_{1}\cdots\int_{\Delta}d\bm{\pi}_{M}\exp\left(t\bar{\pi}\right)\prod_{\alpha=1}^{M}{\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}|\bm{R}_{\alpha})\\
&amp;=\prod_{\alpha=1}^{M}\int_{\Delta}d\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}\exp\left(\frac{t}{M}\sum_{k=0}^{C}w_{k}\pi_{\alpha k}\right){\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}|\bm{R}_{\alpha})\\
&amp;=e^{tw_{0}}\prod_{\alpha=1}^{M}\int_{\Delta}d\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}\exp\left(t\sum_{k=1}^{C}s_{k}\pi_{\alpha k}\right){\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}|\bm{R}_{\alpha}),\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>𝝅</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>𝝅</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>)</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><mi>𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝅</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝑹</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\Phi(t)&amp;=\int_{\Delta}d\bm{\pi}_{1}\cdots\int_{\Delta}d\bm{\pi}_{M}\exp\left(t\bar{\pi}\right)\prod_{\alpha=1}^{M}{\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}|\bm{R}_{\alpha})\\
&amp;=\prod_{\alpha=1}^{M}\int_{\Delta}d\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}\exp\left(\frac{t}{M}\sum_{k=0}^{C}w_{k}\pi_{\alpha k}\right){\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}|\bm{R}_{\alpha})\\
&amp;=e^{tw_{0}}\prod_{\alpha=1}^{M}\int_{\Delta}d\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}\exp\left(t\sum_{k=1}^{C}s_{k}\pi_{\alpha k}\right){\cal P}(\bm{\pi}_{\alpha}|\bm{R}_{\alpha}),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k}\equiv(w_{k}-w_{0})/M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k}\equiv(w_{k}-w_{0})/M</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\alpha 0}=1-\sum_{k=1}^{C}\pi_{\alpha k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\alpha 0}=1-\sum_{k=1}^{C}\pi_{\alpha k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Each integral is the moment-generating function for a Dirichlet distribution, expressed via the confluent Lauricella hypergeometric function <math id="A1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi^{[C]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi^{[C]}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(t)=e^{tw_{0}}\prod_{\alpha=1}^{M}\Psi^{[C]}\left(\nu_{\alpha 1},\ldots,\nu_{\alpha C};T;ts_{1},\ldots,ts_{C}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(t)=e^{tw_{0}}\prod_{\alpha=1}^{M}\Psi^{[C]}\left(\nu_{\alpha 1},\ldots,\nu_{\alpha C};T;ts_{1},\ldots,ts_{C}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Psi^{[C]}\left(\nu_{\alpha 1},\ldots,\nu_{\alpha C};T;ts_{1},\ldots,ts_{C}\right)=\sum_{m_{1}=0}^{\infty}\cdots\sum_{m_{C}=0}^{\infty}\frac{(\nu_{\alpha 1})_{m_{1}}\cdots(\nu_{\alpha C})_{m_{C}}(ts_{1})^{m_{1}}\cdots(ts_{C})^{m_{C}}}{(T)_{m}m_{1}!\cdots m_{C}!}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>!</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi^{[C]}\left(\nu_{\alpha 1},\ldots,\nu_{\alpha C};T;ts_{1},\ldots,ts_{C}\right)=\sum_{m_{1}=0}^{\infty}\cdots\sum_{m_{C}=0}^{\infty}\frac{(\nu_{\alpha 1})_{m_{1}}\cdots(\nu_{\alpha C})_{m_{C}}(ts_{1})^{m_{1}}\cdots(ts_{C})^{m_{C}}}{(T)_{m}m_{1}!\cdots m_{C}!},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p6.3" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x)_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x)_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Pochhammer symbol.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The moments are:</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\Phi^{\prime}(0),\qquad\sigma^{2}=\Phi^{\prime\prime}(0)-(\Phi^{\prime}(0))^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\Phi^{\prime}(0),\qquad\sigma^{2}=\Phi^{\prime\prime}(0)-(\Phi^{\prime}(0))^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Expanding <math id="A1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi^{[C]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi^{[C]}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal O}(t^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal O}(t^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\Psi^{[C]}&amp;=1+\frac{t}{T}\sum_{j=1}^{C}\nu_{\alpha j}s_{j}+\frac{t^{2}}{2T(T+1)}\sum_{j=1}^{C}\nu_{\alpha j}(\nu_{\alpha j}+1)s_{j}^{2}\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{t^{2}}{T(T+1)}\sum_{\ell=1}^{C}\sum_{m=\ell+1}^{C}\nu_{\alpha\ell}\nu_{\alpha m}s_{\ell}s_{m}+{\cal O}(t^{3}).\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msup><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msup><mi>ν</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mi>ν</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\Psi^{[C]}&amp;=1+\frac{t}{T}\sum_{j=1}^{C}\nu_{\alpha j}s_{j}+\frac{t^{2}}{2T(T+1)}\sum_{j=1}^{C}\nu_{\alpha j}(\nu_{\alpha j}+1)s_{j}^{2}\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{t^{2}}{T(T+1)}\sum_{\ell=1}^{C}\sum_{m=\ell+1}^{C}\nu_{\alpha\ell}\nu_{\alpha m}s_{\ell}s_{m}+{\cal O}(t^{3}).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.3" class="ltx_p">Substituting into equation <a href="#A1.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ Appendix A Derivation of Bayesian Estimator and Uncertainty ‣ Don’t Pass@𝑘: A Bayesian Framework for Large Language Model Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> and computing derivatives yields:</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mu&amp;=w_{0}+\frac{1}{MT}\sum_{\alpha=1}^{M}\sum_{j=0}^{C}\nu_{\alpha j}(w_{j}-w_{0}),\\
\sigma^{2}&amp;=\frac{1}{M^{2}(T+1)}\sum_{\alpha=1}^{M}\left\{\sum_{j=0}^{C}\frac{\nu_{\alpha j}}{T}(w_{j}-w_{0})^{2}-\left(\sum_{j=0}^{C}\frac{\nu_{\alpha j}}{T}(w_{j}-w_{0})\right)^{2}\right\}.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mi>μ</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mu&amp;=w_{0}+\frac{1}{MT}\sum_{\alpha=1}^{M}\sum_{j=0}^{C}\nu_{\alpha j}(w_{j}-w_{0}),\\
\sigma^{2}&amp;=\frac{1}{M^{2}(T+1)}\sum_{\alpha=1}^{M}\left\{\sum_{j=0}^{C}\frac{\nu_{\alpha j}}{T}(w_{j}-w_{0})^{2}-\left(\sum_{j=0}^{C}\frac{\nu_{\alpha j}}{T}(w_{j}-w_{0})\right)^{2}\right\}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.4" class="ltx_p">The algorithm summarizing this calculation is shown in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 2.4 Bayesian Estimator and Uncertainty for the Performance Metric ‣ 2 Bayesian Framework for Evaluating LLM Performance ‣ Don’t Pass@𝑘: A Bayesian Framework for Large Language Model Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> in the main text.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Equivalence of Bayesian and Average Rankings for Uniform Prior</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For Bayesian estimators using a uniform prior (where <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1+C+N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1+C+N</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\alpha k}=1+n_{\alpha k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\alpha k}=1+n_{\alpha k}</annotation></semantics></math>), the expression for the mean <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> from equation <a href="#A1.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Appendix A Derivation of Bayesian Estimator and Uncertainty ‣ Don’t Pass@𝑘: A Bayesian Framework for Large Language Model Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> simplifies as:</p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mu&amp;=w_{0}+\frac{1}{M(1+C+N)}\sum_{\alpha=1}^{M}\sum_{j=0}^{C}(1+n_{\alpha j})(w_{j}-w_{0})\\
&amp;=A+\frac{1}{M(1+C+N)}\sum_{\alpha=1}^{M}\sum_{j=0}^{C}w_{j}n_{\alpha j},\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mi>μ</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mu&amp;=w_{0}+\frac{1}{M(1+C+N)}\sum_{\alpha=1}^{M}\sum_{j=0}^{C}(1+n_{\alpha j})(w_{j}-w_{0})\\
&amp;=A+\frac{1}{M(1+C+N)}\sum_{\alpha=1}^{M}\sum_{j=0}^{C}w_{j}n_{\alpha j},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the constant <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\frac{1}{1+C+N}\sum_{j=0}^{C}w_{j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\frac{1}{1+C+N}\sum_{j=0}^{C}w_{j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=0}^{C}n_{\alpha j}=N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=0}^{C}n_{\alpha j}=N</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> relates to a naive weighted average accuracy <math id="A2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> over the number of answers in each category,</p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=\frac{1}{MN}\sum_{\alpha=1}^{M}\sum_{j=0}^{C}w_{j}n_{\alpha j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=\frac{1}{MN}\sum_{\alpha=1}^{M}\sum_{j=0}^{C}w_{j}n_{\alpha j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">via</p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=A+\frac{N}{1+C+N}a." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=A+\frac{N}{1+C+N}a.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Note that in the binary case where <math id="A2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the value of <math id="A2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> is the just regular average accuracy avg@<math id="A2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\!N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\!N</annotation></semantics></math>. For categorical cases, it is just a weighted generalization of avg@<math id="A2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\!N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\!N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is constant across models and the prefactor <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{N}{1+C+N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{N}{1+C+N}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive, we see that if <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu&gt;\mu^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu&gt;\mu^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the corresponding values of <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> from the two methods must always give the same ranking, <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;a^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;a^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Additionally, in the limit of a large number of trials, <math id="A2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that <math id="A2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\approx a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\approx a</annotation></semantics></math>, as expected.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This equivalence extends to uncertainty quantification. The relationship between the standard deviation of the average (<math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\mathrm{avg@}N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>avg</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\mathrm{avg@}N}</annotation></semantics></math>) and the Bayesian standard deviation (<math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\mathrm{Bayes@}N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>Bayes</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\mathrm{Bayes@}N}</annotation></semantics></math> from equation <a href="#A1.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Appendix A Derivation of Bayesian Estimator and Uncertainty ‣ Don’t Pass@𝑘: A Bayesian Framework for Large Language Model Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) is</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\mathrm{avg@}N}=\frac{1+C+N}{N}\sigma_{\mathrm{Bayes@}N}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>avg</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>Bayes</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\mathrm{avg@}N}=\frac{1+C+N}{N}\sigma_{\mathrm{Bayes@}N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The Bayesian expression for <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\mathrm{Bayes@}N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>Bayes</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\mathrm{Bayes@}N}</annotation></semantics></math> is valid for all <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, providing a reliable method to compute uncertainty in avg@<math id="A2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> without relying on the Central Limit Theorem (CLT).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Convergence</h2>

<figure id="A3.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.04265v1/cdf.svg" id="A3.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/332;" width="548" height="332"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Complementing the PMFs in Fig. <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>, these CDFs plot <math id="A3.F5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(k\!\leq\!N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(k\!\leq\!N)</annotation></semantics></math> for the convergence threshold <math id="A3.F5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> across AIME’24, AIME’25, HMMT’25, and BrUMO’25. Steeper and earlier rises indicate faster convergence. Bayes@<math id="A3.F5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\!N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\!N</annotation></semantics></math> accumulates mass with fewer trials than Pass@2/4/8, and on AIME’24/’25 the Pass curves do not reach 1 by <math id="A3.F5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\max}=80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\max}=80</annotation></semantics></math>. Greater convergence suggests that a confidence interval should be included in the evaluation tasks.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Categorical</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As we discussed in Sections  <a href="#S2.SS3" title="2.3 Weighted Performance Metric ‣ 2 Bayesian Framework for Evaluating LLM Performance ‣ Don’t Pass@𝑘: A Bayesian Framework for Large Language Model Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a> and  <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Rubric-Aware Categorical Evaluation ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ Don’t Pass@𝑘: A Bayesian Framework for Large Language Model Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, for each question <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in{1,\ldots,M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in{1,\ldots,M}</annotation></semantics></math>, every attempt yields base signals such as <span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">has_box</span>, <span id="A4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">is_correct</span>, <span id="A4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">token_ratio</span>, <span id="A4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">prompt_bpt</span>, <span id="A4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">completion_bpt</span>, and verifier probabilities <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B,C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B,C</annotation></semantics></math> for <em id="A4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">correct</em>, <em id="A4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">wrong</em>, and <em id="A4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">invalid/off-task</em>. Using thresholds and Boolean criteria, each attempt is mapped into one of <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C+1</annotation></semantics></math> categories under a chosen schema (e.g., <em id="A4.p1.1.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Format Aware</em>, <em id="A4.p1.1.10" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Conf-Wrong Penalty</em>, <em id="A4.p1.1.11" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Efficiency-Adjusted</em>; Table <a href="#A4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Selected categorical schema. ‣ Appendix D Categorical ‣ Don’t Pass@𝑘: A Bayesian Framework for Large Language Model Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). We instantiate categorical schemata and update posterior means via Dirichlet–multinomial inference, yielding metrics that preserve correctness while explicitly reflecting formatting, calibration, and efficiency.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Base signals</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All signals are directly obtainable from common LLM inference stacks such as Hugging Face transformers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wolf et al. [2019]</a></cite> and vLLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwon et al. [2023b]</a></cite>, via per-step scores/log-probs and termination metadata, and require no model-specific instrumentation; the verifier probabilities
A, B, C are defined in  <a href="#A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" title="Reward models in evaluation. ‣ Appendix D Categorical ‣ Don’t Pass@𝑘: A Bayesian Framework for Large Language Model Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">has_box</span>: 1 if a final boxed answer is present; else 0.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">is_correct</span>: 1 if the answer is correct; else 0.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">token_ratio</span>: completion tokens normalized by 32,768 (shorter is smaller).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">repeated_pattern</span>: 0 if <span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">finish_reason</span> is <span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">stop</span>; else 1 (degenerate output).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">prompt_bpt</span>: negative average prompt log-prob in bits/token (lower is better).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">completion_bpt</span>: negative average completion log-prob in bits/token (lower is better).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">compass_context_A</span>: verifier contextual probability of <em id="A4.I1.i7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">correct</em>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">compass_context_B</span>: verifier contextual probability of <em id="A4.I1.i8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">wrong</em>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">compass_context_C</span>: verifier contextual probability of <em id="A4.I1.i9.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">irrelevant/off-task</em>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reward models in evaluation.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While reward models are most familiar from fine-tuning (e.g., RLHF), we use one as a <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">lightweight verifier</em> to supply per-attempt label probabilities for</p>
<table id="A4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A,B,C\}=\{\text{correct},\text{wrong},\text{invalid/off-task}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>correct</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>wrong</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>invalid/off-task</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A,B,C\}=\{\text{correct},\text{wrong},\text{invalid/off-task}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">in evaluation. Concretely, we employ OpenCompass <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CompassVerifier-3B</span> to produce <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,B,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,B,C)</annotation></semantics></math> and then apply <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">contextual calibration</em> to obtain a more robust, prompt-stable label distribution: we evaluate next-token scores for the candidate labels at a fixed answer slot, subtract a content-free baseline logit <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> from the task logit <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> for each label <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, and apply temperature scaling to yield calibrated probabilities</p>
<table id="A4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(y\mid x)=\mathrm{softmax}\!\left(\frac{s_{y}-b_{y}}{T}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:3.720em;" width="3.720em"><mi>softmax</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(y\mid x)=\mathrm{softmax}\!\left(\frac{s_{y}-b_{y}}{T}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This helps us mitigate saturation and the entanglement of formatting and confidence seen with last-token probabilities, and improves probability calibration for downstream rubric scoring.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Selected categorical schema.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define 12 schemata (Table <a href="#A4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Selected categorical schema. ‣ Appendix D Categorical ‣ Don’t Pass@𝑘: A Bayesian Framework for Large Language Model Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) using the rubric variables (Table <a href="#A4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Selected categorical schema. ‣ Appendix D Categorical ‣ Don’t Pass@𝑘: A Bayesian Framework for Large Language Model Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) derived from the base signals; here are two illustrative definitions (the others follow analogously):</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A4.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Format Aware</span>:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{cat}=\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{invalid}\\
1&amp;\text{wrong}\wedge\text{unboxed}\\
2&amp;\text{wrong}\wedge\text{boxed}\\
3&amp;\text{correct}\wedge\text{unboxed}\\
4&amp;\text{correct}\wedge\text{boxed}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>cat</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>invalid</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>wrong</mtext><mo>∧</mo><mtext>unboxed</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>wrong</mtext><mo>∧</mo><mtext>boxed</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>correct</mtext><mo>∧</mo><mtext>unboxed</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>correct</mtext><mo>∧</mo><mtext>boxed</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{cat}=\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{invalid}\\
1&amp;\text{wrong}\wedge\text{unboxed}\\
2&amp;\text{wrong}\wedge\text{boxed}\\
3&amp;\text{correct}\wedge\text{unboxed}\\
4&amp;\text{correct}\wedge\text{boxed}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conf-Wrong Penalty</span>:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{cat}=\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{invalid}\\
1&amp;\text{wrong}_{\text{high\_conf}}\\
2&amp;\text{wrong}\wedge\text{low\_conf}\\
3&amp;\text{correct}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>cat</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>invalid</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mtext>wrong</mtext><mtext>high_conf</mtext></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>wrong</mtext><mo>∧</mo><mtext>low_conf</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>correct</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{cat}=\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{invalid}\\
1&amp;\text{wrong}_{\text{high\_conf}}\\
2&amp;\text{wrong}\wedge\text{low\_conf}\\
3&amp;\text{correct}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Rubric weights <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}</annotation></semantics></math> are chosen to reflect evaluation preferences. For example, <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Format Aware</em> might use <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,0,1,2,3]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,0,1,2,3]</annotation></semantics></math> to mildly reward formatting when correct and slightly penalize confidently wrong (via schema choice); <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Efficiency-Adjusted</em> can downweight verbose outputs among both correct and wrong categories.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A4.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Exact Match</span>   Correctness only; ignores formatting, confidence, and length.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Format Aware</span>   Rewards boxed, well-formatted answers; distinguishes boxed/unboxed even when wrong.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conf-Calibrated</span>   Penalizes <em id="A4.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">confidently wrong</em>; grades correct answers by confidence (low/mid/high).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OOD Robustness</span>   Separates in-distribution vs. OOD prompts; checks correctness under both.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I3.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Strict Compliance</span>   Requires boxed final answers; unboxed-correct is treated as non-compliant.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I3.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conf-Wrong Penalty</span>   Heavier penalty for wrong answers at high confidence; lighter when uncertain.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I3.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Verifier-Only</span>   Uses verifier signals (A/B/C) alone to rank; model-agnostic probe of the verifier.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I3.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Format+Confidence</span>   Balanced composite over (boxed/unboxed) <math id="A4.I3.i8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> (low/high confidence) for both wrong and correct; emphasizes boxed, high-confidence correctness and penalizes confidently wrong.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I3.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Length-Robust</span>   Isolates correctness irrespective of verbosity; does not penalize length.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i10" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I3.i10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Verifier Prob</span>   Probes agreement with the verifier: flags wrong with high verifier <em id="A4.I3.i10.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">A</em> as inconsistent and distinguishes under/over-confidence on correct.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i11" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I3.i11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Efficiency-Adjusted</span>   Rewards short, correct completions; penalizes verbose outputs (especially when wrong).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i12" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.i12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Concise High-Conf</span>   Prefers concise, high-confidence correct answers; downweights verbose correctness.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Rubric variables, decision formulas, and brief descriptions used to map each model attempt into discrete categories. Thresholds (<math id="A4.T4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{high}},\tau_{\text{low\_wrong}},\tau_{\text{prompt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>high</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>low_wrong</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>prompt</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{high}},\tau_{\text{low\_wrong}},\tau_{\text{prompt}}</annotation></semantics></math>) and length quantiles (<math id="A4.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{len\_p33},\text{len\_p66}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>len_p33</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>len_p66</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{len\_p33},\text{len\_p66}</annotation></semantics></math>) are computed per dataset from observed bits-per-token and token-ratio statistics. Category <math id="A4.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> is reserved for invalid outputs (degenerate repetition or high verifier <math id="A4.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>), and <math id="A4.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B,C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B,C</annotation></semantics></math> denote calibrated verifier probabilities for <em id="A4.T4.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">correct</em>, <em id="A4.T4.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">wrong</em>, and <em id="A4.T4.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">off-task</em>, respectively.</figcaption>
<table id="A4.T4.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A4.T4.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T4.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rubric variables</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T4.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Formula</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T4.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Description</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">invalid</td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A4.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{repeated\_pattern}=1)\lor(C\geq 0.50)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>repeated_pattern</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{repeated\_pattern}=1)\lor(C\geq 0.50)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Category 0 reserved for invalid.</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">correct</td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{is\_correct}\geq 0.5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>is_correct</mtext><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{is\_correct}\geq 0.5)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Boolean mask of correctness.</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">wrong</td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{is\_correct}&lt;0.5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>is_correct</mtext><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{is\_correct}&lt;0.5)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Complement of correct.</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">high_conf</td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{completion\_bpt}\leq\tau_{\text{high}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>completion_bpt</mtext><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>high</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{completion\_bpt}\leq\tau_{\text{high}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Confidence proxy</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">low_conf</td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{completion\_bpt}&gt;\tau_{\text{high}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>completion_bpt</mtext><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>high</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{completion\_bpt}&gt;\tau_{\text{high}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Complement of high_conf.</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">wrong_high_conf</td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">wrong <math id="A4.T4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A4.T4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{completion\_bpt}\leq\tau_{\text{low\_wrong}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>completion_bpt</mtext><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>low_wrong</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{completion\_bpt}\leq\tau_{\text{low\_wrong}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Penalize confidently wrong.</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">ood</td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{prompt\_bpt}\geq\tau_{\text{prompt}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>prompt_bpt</mtext><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>prompt</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{prompt\_bpt}\geq\tau_{\text{prompt}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Out-of-distribution prompt.</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">ind</td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{prompt\_bpt}&lt;\tau_{\text{prompt}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>prompt_bpt</mtext><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>prompt</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{prompt\_bpt}&lt;\tau_{\text{prompt}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">In-distribution prompt.</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">economical</td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{token\_ratio}\leq\text{len\_p33})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>token_ratio</mtext><mo>≤</mo><mtext>len_p33</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{token\_ratio}\leq\text{len\_p33})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Short completions.</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">moderate</td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{len\_p33}&lt;\text{token\_ratio}\leq\text{len\_p66})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>len_p33</mtext><mo>&lt;</mo><mtext>token_ratio</mtext><mo>≤</mo><mtext>len_p66</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{len\_p33}&lt;\text{token\_ratio}\leq\text{len\_p66})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Medium-length completions.</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">verbose</td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{token\_ratio}&gt;\text{len\_p66})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>token_ratio</mtext><mo>&gt;</mo><mtext>len_p66</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{token\_ratio}&gt;\text{len\_p66})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.12.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Long completions.</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.13" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">boxed</td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{has\_box}\geq 0.5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>has_box</mtext><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{has\_box}\geq 0.5)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.13.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Answer is boxed.</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.14" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.14.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">unboxed</td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.14.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{has\_box}&lt;0.5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>has_box</mtext><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{has\_box}&lt;0.5)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.14.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Answer is not boxed.</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.15" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.15.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">A_high</td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.15.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A\geq 0.6)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A\geq 0.6)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.15.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Verifier confidence high.</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.16" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.16.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{high}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>high</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{high}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.16.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">40th percentile of <span id="A4.T4.5.16.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">completion_bpt</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.16.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.17" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.17.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{low\_wrong}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>low_wrong</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{low\_wrong}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.17.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">60th percentile of <span id="A4.T4.5.17.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">completion_bpt</span> among wrong items</td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.17.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.18" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.18.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{prompt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>prompt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{prompt}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.18.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">90th percentile of <span id="A4.T4.5.18.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">prompt_bpt</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.18.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.19" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.19.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T4.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{len\_p33},\,\text{len\_p66}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>len_p33</mtext><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mtext>len_p66</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{len\_p33},\,\text{len\_p66}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.19.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">33rd and 66th percentiles of <span id="A4.T4.5.19.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">token_ratio</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.19.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.20" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.20.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><math id="A4.T4.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{corr\_p33},\,\text{corr\_p66}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>corr_p33</mtext><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mtext>corr_p66</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{corr\_p33},\,\text{corr\_p66}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.20.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">33rd and 66th percentiles of <span id="A4.T4.5.20.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">completion_bpt</span> correct items</td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.20.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_border_bb"></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Definitions of the twelve categorical evaluation schemata used in our Dirichlet–multinomial framework. Each schema specifies decision rules over correctness, formatting (boxed/unboxed), confidence (via <span id="A4.T5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">completion_bpt</span>), prompt distribution (in-distribution vs. OOD), output economy (via <span id="A4.T5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">token_ratio</span>), and verifier signals <math id="A4.T5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,B,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,B,C)</annotation></semantics></math>. These rules map every attempt into <math id="A4.T5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C{+}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C{+}1</annotation></semantics></math> discrete categories, enabling posterior means and credible intervals for any chosen weight vector <math id="A4.T5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
<table id="A4.T5.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A4.T5.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T5.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T5.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Categorical Schema</span></td>
<td id="A4.T5.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A4.T5.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A4.T5.4.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.T5.4.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rubric</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T5.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
