<td id="A4.T5.4.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Format+Confidence</td>
<td id="A4.T5.4.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">
<span id="A4.T5.4.9.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A4.T5.4.9.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">0 invalid; 1 wrong <math id="A4.T5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> unboxed; 2 wrong <math id="A4.T5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> boxed <math id="A4.T5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> low_conf; 3 wrong <math id="A4.T5.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> boxed <math id="A4.T5.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> high_conf; 4 correct <math id="A4.T5.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> unboxed <math id="A4.T5.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> low_conf; 5 correct <math id="A4.T5.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> unboxed <math id="A4.T5.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> high_conf; 6 correct <math id="A4.T5.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> boxed <math id="A4.T5.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> low_conf; 7 correct <math id="A4.T5.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> boxed <math id="A4.T5.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> high_conf</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T5.4.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T5.4.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Length-Robust</td>
<td id="A4.T5.4.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">
<span id="A4.T5.4.10.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A4.T5.4.10.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">0 invalid; 1 wrong; 2 correct</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T5.4.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T5.4.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Verifier Probe</td>
<td id="A4.T5.4.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">
<span id="A4.T5.4.11.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A4.T5.4.11.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">0 invalid; 1 wrong <math id="A4.T5.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> A_high; 2 wrong <math id="A4.T5.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A4.T5.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lnot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>¬</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lnot</annotation></semantics></math> A_high; 3 correct <math id="A4.T5.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A4.T5.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lnot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>¬</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lnot</annotation></semantics></math> A_high; 4 correct <math id="A4.T5.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> A_high</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T5.4.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T5.4.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Efficiency-Adjusted</td>
<td id="A4.T5.4.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">
<span id="A4.T5.4.12.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A4.T5.4.12.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">0 invalid; 1 wrong <math id="A4.T5.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> economical; 2 wrong <math id="A4.T5.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> moderate; 3 wrong <math id="A4.T5.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> verbose; 4 correct <math id="A4.T5.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> economical; 5 correct <math id="A4.T5.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> moderate; 6 correct <math id="A4.T5.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> verbose</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T5.4.13" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T5.4.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Concision-High-Conf</td>
<td id="A4.T5.4.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">
<span id="A4.T5.4.13.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A4.T5.4.13.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">0 invalid; 1 wrong; 2 correct <math id="A4.T5.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> verbose; 3 correct <math id="A4.T5.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> moderate; 4 correct <math id="A4.T5.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> economical; 5 correct <math id="A4.T5.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> economical <math id="A4.T5.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math> high_conf</span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.04265v1/Categorical_ranking.svg" id="A4.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/417;" width="548" height="417"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Competition ranks by model across selected categorical schema. Each column is a combination of base signals; lines indicate how a model’s relative position shifts when the rubric changes.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A4.F6" title="In Selected categorical schema. ‣ Appendix D Categorical ‣ Don’t Pass@𝑘: A Bayesian Framework for Large Language Model Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> summarizes aggregated results across tasks. The leader <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/qwen.png" id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> Qwen3-30B-A3B-Thinking ranks first under all selected schema, but the margin to rank 2 depends on the rubric (largest under <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Conf-Wrong Penalty</em>, smallest under <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Verifier-Only</em>. Mid-pack reorderings are rubric) sensitive: under <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Verifier Prob</em>, <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/openthinker.png" id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">OpenThinker2-32B</em> edges <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.7.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.7.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/chatgpt.png" id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.8" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">gpt-oss-20b_medium</em>; under calibration-heavy category (e.g., <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Conf-Calibrated</em>, <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.10" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Format+Confidence</em>), <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.11.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.11.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.11.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/chatgpt.png" id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.12" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">gpt-oss-20b_high</em> overtakes <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.13.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.13.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.13.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/openthinker.png" id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.g5" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.14" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">OpenThinker2-32B</em>; <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.15" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">OOD Robustness</em> narrows the gap between ranks 2 and 3. Several categories (<em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.16" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Format Aware</em>, <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.17" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Length-Robust</em>, <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.18" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Strict Compliance</em>) agree closely, indicating that once correctness is accounted for, formatting and length rarely flip top ranks. In contrast, calibration-focused categories emphasize and penalize confidently wrong behavior, and efficiency-oriented categories favor concision. The lower tier is stable across categories (<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.19" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.19.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.19.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.19.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/lg.png" id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.g6" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.20" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">EXAONE-4.0-1.2B</em>, <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.21" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.21.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.21.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.21.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/openthinker.png" id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.g7" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.22" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">OpenThinker3-1.5B</em>, <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.23" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:1.4pt;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.23.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:5.8pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.23.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.23.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/Nvidia.png" id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.g8" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:12/8;" width="12" height="8" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.24" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">OpenReasoning-Nemotron-1.5B</em>, <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.25" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.25.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.25.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.25.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/sky.jpeg" id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.g9" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.26" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Sky-T1-32B-Flash</em>, <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.27" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.27.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.27.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.27.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/deepseek.png" id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.g10" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.28" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-1.5B</em>), suggesting rubric choice primarily reshuffles the middle while preserving extremes. Overall, the categorical schema surfaces complementary facets—format compliance, calibration, efficiency, OOD robustness, and verifier alignment—making rubric-dependent differences explicit and enabling compute-efficient, uncertainty-aware comparisons aligned with evaluation goals.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Extended Related Work</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The evaluation of LLMs in generative reasoning tasks, under test-time scaling (e.g., via repeated sampling<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Brown et al. [2024]</a></cite>), has evolved to address the stochastic nature of inference and the need for robust measures of functional correctness. Early approaches relied on syntactic similarity metrics like BLEU <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">Papineni et al. [2002]</a></cite> and CodeBLEU <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ren et al. [2020]</a></cite>, which compare generated answers against reference solutions. However, these metrics often fail to capture semantic correctness in reasoning tasks, motivating metrics based on execution-validation or test-based validation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kulal et al. [2019]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ren et al. [2020]</a></cite>. This limitation has shifted focus toward functional evaluation, where the generated solution is assessed via a ground truth to verify correctness<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kulal et al. [2019]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks et al. [2021b]</a></cite>. In this section, we review key functional metrics, focusing on those that leverage multiple samples to scale performance at inference time. These metrics form the basis to assess LLM capabilities but often overlook probabilistic uncertainty or consistency across samples, motivating our novel Bayesian framework.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The Pass@<math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> metric</span>, originally introduced by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kulal et al. [2019]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. [2021b]</a></cite> for evaluating LLMs trained on code. It measures the probability that at least one of <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> independently generated samples for a given problem passes all associated unit tests (i.e., by matching ground-truth answers or satisfying logical constraints), offering a practical estimate of a model’s potential performance in solving a variety of complex tasks and problems. The unbiased estimator of Pass@<math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is computed as:</p>
<table id="A5.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Pass@}k=\mathbb{E}_{\text{problems}}\left[1-\frac{\binom{n-c}{k}}{\binom{n}{k}}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Pass@</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mtext>problems</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Pass@}k=\mathbb{E}_{\text{problems}}\left[1-\frac{\binom{n-c}{k}}{\binom{n}{k}}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of generated samples and <math id="A5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of correct solutions within the <math id="A5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> trials. This estimator has smaller uncertainty in the limit of <math id="A5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\gg k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≫</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\gg k</annotation></semantics></math>, ensuring reliable approximations. However, due to computational costs, <math id="A5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is often comparable to <math id="A5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> in practice, which can increase variance and weaken evaluation stability. The Pass@<math id="A5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> metric has been adapted beyond code to evaluate LLMs in various tasks requiring verifiable correctness, such as math, logic, and general reasoning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks et al. [2021b]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib75" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al. [2021]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib76" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. [2022]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib77" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lewkowycz et al. [2022]</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pass</span>ˆ<math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, introduced in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yao et al. [2024]</a></cite>, extends the Pass@<math id="A5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> metric to capture both the potential performance and the consistency of LLMs in reasoning tasks, where evaluating the reliability and stability of generated solutions is crucial. Passˆ<math id="A5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the probability that all <math id="A5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> trials are correct:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A5.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Pass\^{}}k=\mathbb{E}_{\text{problems}}\left[\frac{\binom{c}{k}}{\binom{n}{k}}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Passˆ</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mtext>problems</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Pass\^{}}k=\mathbb{E}_{\text{problems}}\left[\frac{\binom{c}{k}}{\binom{n}{k}}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> retain the same meanings as in Pass@<math id="A5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. This metric assumes that all the trials are independent and uniformly distributed, approximating the binomial distribution with a hypergeometric distribution to account for sampling without replacement. By requiring all <math id="A5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> samples to be correct, Passˆ<math id="A5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> provides a stringent measure of model consistency and stability.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">To introduce flexibility, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. [2024a]</a></cite> proposed <span id="A5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">G-Pass@<math id="A5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\tilde{\tau}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\tilde{\tau}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>, which incorporates a tolerance threshold <math id="A5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\tau}\in(0.0,1.0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\tau}\in(0.0,1.0]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{G-Pass@}k_{\tilde{\tau}}=\mathbb{E}_{\text{problems}}\left[\sum_{j=\lceil\tau\cdot k\rceil}^{c}\frac{\binom{c}{j}\cdot\binom{n-c}{k-j}}{\binom{n}{k}}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>G-Pass@</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mtext>problems</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{G-Pass@}k_{\tilde{\tau}}=\mathbb{E}_{\text{problems}}\left[\sum_{j=\lceil\tau\cdot k\rceil}^{c}\frac{\binom{c}{j}\cdot\binom{n-c}{k-j}}{\binom{n}{k}}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil\tau\cdot k\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil\tau\cdot k\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> is the smallest integer greater than or equal to <math id="A5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\cdot k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\cdot k</annotation></semantics></math>. This formulation allows up to <math id="A5.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k-\lceil\tau\cdot k\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k-\lceil\tau\cdot k\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> incorrect solutions, balancing the assessment of potential with consistency. As a special case, Pass@<math id="A5.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to G-Pass@<math id="A5.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> in the limit <math id="A5.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. [2024a]</a></cite> introduced <span id="A5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">mG-Pass@<math id="A5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></span>, an interpolated metric that integrates G-Pass@<math id="A5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in[0.5,1.0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in[0.5,1.0]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{mG-Pass@}k=2\int_{0.5}^{1.0}\text{G-Pass@}k_{\tau}d\tau\approx\frac{2}{k}\sum_{i=\lceil 0.5\cdot k\rceil+1}^{k}\text{G-Pass@}k_{i/k}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>mG-Pass@</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mn>1.0</mn></msubsup><mrow><mtext>G-Pass@</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><mtext>G-Pass@</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{mG-Pass@}k=2\int_{0.5}^{1.0}\text{G-Pass@}k_{\tau}d\tau\approx\frac{2}{k}\sum_{i=\lceil 0.5\cdot k\rceil+1}^{k}\text{G-Pass@}k_{i/k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p6.2" class="ltx_p">providing a more comprehensive measure that jointly reflects performance potential and reasoning stability.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p7.1" class="ltx_p">These extended metrics have been applied to mathematical reasoning benchmarks such as LiveMathBench, MATH, and AIME, where they reveal substantial performance degradation of LLMs under stricter stability requirements.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Experiment setup and Reproducibility</h2>

<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Metrics</h3>

<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Kendall’s Tau:</h5>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Kendall’s tau (<math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>) is a nonparametric rank correlation coefficient that quantifies the ordinal relationship between two ranked sets by evaluating the consistency in their orderings. For two rankings of <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> items, it examines all unique pairs <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;j</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A pair is <em id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">concordant</em> if the relative ordering of items <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> is the same in both rankings (both place <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> before <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> or vice versa).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A pair is <em id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">discordant</em> if the relative ordering is different.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Pairs with ties in either ranking are neither concordant nor discordant.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> as the number of concordant pairs, <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> as the number of discordant pairs, and <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{0}=n(n-1)/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{0}=n(n-1)/2</annotation></semantics></math> as the total number of unique pairs. Let <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the number of tied pairs in the first ranking, and <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> similarly for the second ranking.
The two common variants are the following:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A6.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Tau-a:}\quad\tau_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Tau-a:</mtext><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Tau-a:}\quad\tau_{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E25.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{n_{c}-n_{d}}{n_{0}}\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\text{(no adjustment for ties)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mtext>(no adjustment for ties)</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{n_{c}-n_{d}}{n_{0}}\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\text{(no adjustment for ties)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Tau-b:}\quad\tau_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Tau-b:</mtext><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Tau-b:}\quad\tau_{b}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E26.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{n_{c}-n_{d}}{\sqrt{(n_{0}-n_{1})(n_{0}-n_{2})}}\qquad\text{(adjusts for ties in both rankings)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mtext>(adjusts for ties in both rankings)</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{n_{c}-n_{d}}{\sqrt{(n_{0}-n_{1})(n_{0}-n_{2})}}\qquad\text{(adjusts for ties in both rankings)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Tau-a assumes no ties and may underestimate correlation when ties occur. Tau-b, which corrects for ties, is better suited for datasets with equivalent rankings.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In our implementation, we use <span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">scipy.stats.kendalltau</span> with its default variant=’b’, which computes <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> efficiently and handles ties appropriately. The coefficient ranges from <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math> (perfect disagreement) to <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+1</annotation></semantics></math> (perfect agreement), with <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> indicating no association. This metric provides a robust, distribution-free measure for comparing model performance rankings, particularly when ties reflect meaningful equivalences.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Models and Datasets</h3>

<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Datasets.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate on four math–reasoning test sets: AIME’24 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mathematical Association of America [2024]</a></cite>, AIME’25 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mathematical Association of America [2025]</a></cite>, BrUMO’25 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Brown University Math Olympiad Organizers [2025]</a></cite>, and HMMT’25 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Harvard–MIT Mathematics Tournament [2025]</a></cite>. AIME is administered by the Mathematical Association of America and consists of two sets of 15 integer-answer problems; we use the 2024 and 2025 problem sets. For HMMT’25, we use the officially posted February 2025 contest set (algebra, geometry, number theory, and combinatorics). For BrUMO’25, we use the published 2025 problem sets from the tournament archive.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Models.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unless noted otherwise, we run each generator with the provider-recommended chat template (DeepSeek/Qwen style when unspecified) and identical decoding settings (below) to minimize template-induced variance. The model cohort includes:
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/sky.jpeg" id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> Sky-T1-32B-Flash <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib78" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team [2025a]</a></cite> (reasoning-optimized “flash” variant tied to overthinking-reduction work),
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/qwen.png" id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> Qwen3-30B-A3B-Thinking-2507 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib79" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team [2025b]</a></cite> (Qwen3 series, reasoning variant),
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/deepseek.png" id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-1.5B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al. [2025]</a></cite> (distilled reasoning model), <span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/chatgpt.png" id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> <span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text">gpt-oss-20b</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib80" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI [2025]</a></cite> (OpenAI open-weight reasoning model; we use the default quantization, MXFP4. For prompting, we rely on OpenAI Harmony, which defines three levels of reasoning efforts. <span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.6.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.6.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/gair.png" id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.g5" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> LIMO-v2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib81" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ye et al. [2025]</a></cite> (data-efficient reasoning fine-tuned on curated traces),
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.7.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.7.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/lg.png" id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.g6" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> EXAONE-4.0-1.2B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib82" title="" class="ltx_ref">LG AI Research [2025]</a></cite> (hybrid non-reasoning/reasoning modes),
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:1.4pt;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.8.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:5.8pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.8.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/Nvidia.png" id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.g7" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:12/8;" width="12" height="8" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> OpenReasoning-Nemotron-1.5B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib83" title="" class="ltx_ref">Toshniwal et al. [2025]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib84" title="" class="ltx_ref">Moshkov et al. [2025]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib85" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ahmad et al. [2025a]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib86" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ahmad et al. [2025b]</a></cite> (open-weight small reasoning model),
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.9.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.9.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.9.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/openthinker.png" id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.g8" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> OpenThinker2-32B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib87" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guha et al. [2025]</a></cite> and <span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.10.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.10.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.10.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/openthinker.png" id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.g9" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> OpenThinker3-1.5B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib87" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guha et al. [2025]</a></cite> (trained on OpenThoughts2/3 data recipes).
For verification we additionally use <span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.11.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.11.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.11.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/compass.png" id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.g10" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> CompassVerifier-3B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib88" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. [2025b]</a></cite>, a lightweight answer verifier suitable for outcome reward and equivalence checking.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prompting.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For most models, we follow the provider-recommended DeepSeek/Qwen-style prompt:
<em id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">“Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within <span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">\boxed<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">{}</span></span>.”</em> For <span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/chatgpt.png" id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> <span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gpt-oss-20b</span>, we instead use the OpenAI Harmony prompt template, which provides three levels of reasoning effort. For <span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:1.4pt;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:5.8pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/Nvidia.png" id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:12/8;" width="12" height="8" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> <span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">OpenReasoning-Nemotron-1.5B</span>, we adopt the task-specific prompt:
<em id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">“Solve the following math problem. Make sure to put the answer (and only the answer) inside <span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">\boxed<span id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">{}</span></span>.”</em></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Reproducibility</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A6.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sampling setup.</span> All trials use top-<math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> sampling with temperature <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.6</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.95</annotation></semantics></math>, batch size <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, and seeds <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1234" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1234</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1234</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1313" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1313</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1313</annotation></semantics></math>. We perform <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=80</annotation></semantics></math> trials per dataset/model.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Serving stack.</span> Token generation is served with <span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">vLLM</span> (PagedAttention) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwon et al. [2023b]</a></cite>, and models are loaded in <span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bf16</span> unless the release requires MXFP4 (e.g., <span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gpt-oss</span>). We record log-probabilities for both the input prompt and generated tokens, and cap <span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">max_tokens</span> at <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32{,}768" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32,768</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32{,}768</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Verifier.</span> We use <span id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.0pt;">
<span id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:8.7pt;height:8.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2510.04265v1/Figures/models/compass.png" id="A6.I2.i3.p1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:12/12;" width="12" height="12" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
</span></span></span> <span id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CompassVerifier-3B</span> as a reward model. During evaluation, we leverage the model’s scores on prompts generated by other models to create categorical schemas. We rely on the <span id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Transformers</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wolf et al. [2019]</a></cite> and <span id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Accelerate</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib89" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gugger et al. [2022]</a></cite> libraries. To maximize throughput, we enable FlashAttention kernels <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dao [2023]</a></cite> and adopt the <span id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DFloat11</span> format <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib90" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. [2025b]</a></cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hardware.</span> All runs execute on clusters with <math id="A6.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\times</annotation></semantics></math> NVIDIA H200 (141GB).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
